# Optional: without a key, the assistant answers from site search (the best
# passage, verbatim, with its source).
# Keep real keys in .env.local or the hosting provider's environment settings.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional model override; unset uses gemini-3.5-flash-lite. Must be a Gemini 3
# or later model that accepts the MINIMAL thinking level. gemini-3.5-flash was
# measured against it (2026-11-17, spec/AI_ASSISTANT.md §8): it stalled or
# returned 503s on most calls and hit its free-tier quota after 21 requests.
GEMINI_MODEL=

# Canonical public origin for metadata, sitemap, and social previews.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://mubin-attar.vercel.app

# Per-instance daily limit on model calls. Every call counts: an answer, its
# hedged second call when the first is slow, and a routing call.
ASSISTANT_DAILY_CAP=500

# Optional: model calls one visitor may cause per UTC day (1–20000). Unset uses
# 30 in production. Under `next dev` it is lifted to ASSISTANT_DAILY_CAP, since
# every local request is the same visitor, so local review is never blocked by
# it; set it here to test the per-visitor limit locally.
# ASSISTANT_CLIENT_DAILY_LIMIT=30

# Optional booking link on /hire. Unset uses the Cal.com URL in config/site.ts;
# any value that is not an absolute http(s) URL, including an empty one, hides it.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CAL_URL=https://cal.com/your-handle

# Optional newsletter form at the foot of /writing and /notes: the Buttondown
# handle it posts to. Unset or empty hides the form. Set it only once the list is
# confirmed to deliver to new subscribers.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BUTTONDOWN_USERNAME=your-buttondown-handle
